  "title": "fix round 1 for T-1406: restore rerun candidate extraction so argument-like ids stay audited as rejected",
  "spec": "Why: T-1406's gate went red on tests/test_daemon.py test_rerun_rejects_argument_like_ids: resume_hint.rejected_ids lost '--rootdir=/'. Besides the requested quota change, T-1406 changed failures._test_id_candidates to keep only _TEST_ID_TOKEN matches from a FAILED line, so argument-like tokens are no longer candidates and are no longer recorded as rejected. That audit is a safety property (argument injection into the rerun command); the spec never asked to change candidate extraction.\n\nWhat (in wt/T-1406 on task/T-1406, on top of its commit): restore _test_id_candidates to the original split (line[7:].split(\" - \", 1)[0].split()) so every token is a candidate and invalid ones land in rejected_ids as before. Keep everything else from T-1406: _TEST_ID_TOKEN used only by _strip_test_ids, _QUOTA_MARKER with word boundaries, the gate_red skip of the quota branch, and tests/test_failures.py::test_gate_red_with_cooling_test_id_is_not_quota.\n\nCommit, then run tests/test_failures.py and tests/test_daemon.py -k \"rerun or quota or failure_kind\" in the foreground. Never background a command, never the full gate.",
